Commands marked `available` run via the CLI at `{{scripts_path}}` — the version
this skill was installed with, so the CLI and these rules always agree.

`update` is the exception: its job is to move that version forward, so run it
as `{{update_path}} update`. Run pinned, it refreshes to the version already
installed and reports success for a no-op.

Commands marked `planned` are listed for context only — running one errors out,
since it is not yet registered.

## Reading command output

Consume the full output of any Jig command. Never pipe it through `head`, `tail`,
`grep`, or `jq` — findings are ordered by severity, not by position, and
truncating drops the ones that matter.

If a command's output is already in this session's history and no files have
changed since, do not re-run it.

