## Attestation

Before you finish a task that generated or modified UI, emit this line:

```text
JIG_CHECK: version=<version> mode=<mode> mechanical=<pass|fail|skipped>:<n> judgment=<ran|skipped> files=<n> styled=<n>
```

`jig check` emits this same line for the half it can do, with
`judgment=not-run`. Take `mechanical=` from its output rather than counting by
hand; fill `judgment=` yourself. If `check` could not run at all, that is
`mechanical=skipped:0` — never `pass`, which would report a clean result for a
check that never inspected anything.

A skipped check must say `skipped` and give the reason. Do not report `ran` for
a check you did not perform.

**`files=` and `styled=` describe a scope, and the scope is not fixed.**
`jig check` defaults to the files changed since HEAD and falls back to the
whole repo only when that diff is empty. So the same project reports a
different `files=` before and after a commit with nothing else having moved,
and two `JIG_CHECK:` lines are comparable only when both runs had the same
scope. Run `jig check --all` for a number that describes the project rather
than your diff — `--all` widens the files, not the rules. A narrowed run says
so in its own output; attest from what it printed, not from what you assumed
it looked at.
